  "worked_solution": "If the difference between the actual time and the time shown on the clock is $T$ seconds, then the rate of the change of this difference is $\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in weeks.\n\nSince the difference *increases* by $30$ seconds each week, the rate of change of the difference is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=30.\n$$",
